feat(auth): site-wide sign-in gate for the-dump-bin.com

Promote the EOD-only auth from /EOD/ to the whole hub so a single sign-in
covers every Retail Odyssey tool here (EOD, claims, suncare, shirt-order,
dump-bin, furniture, view.html). Replaces what Cloudflare Access used to
do at the edge.

- auth-gate.js (new) — shared boot guard included at the top of every
  gated page. Reads localStorage.dumpBinSession; redirects to
  /signin.html if missing. On a magic-link ?token= it calls
  /api/verify-token, stores the session JWT, strips the token from the
  URL. Hides the body until the exchange resolves so users don't see a
  flash. Exposes window.dumpBinAuthFetch (Bearer-fortified fetch with
  noBounceOn401 escape hatch for SAS-style 401s) and window.dumpBinSignOut.
  Migrates the older localStorage.eodSession key transparently.
- signin.html (new at hub root) — request-link form + access-request
  overlay. Generalized copy ("Sign in to The Dump Bin"). Bounces an
  already-signed-in user to / (or back to ?next=) instead of /EOD/.
- admin.html (new at hub root) — same first-time setup / login / forgot
  / reset / allowlist CRUD flow as the previous /EOD/admin.html, with
  dumpBinAdminSession key (migrated from eodAdminSession).
- EOD/index.html — replaced with the in-flight Phase B build (was
  pre-Phase-B in this repo), then taught to consume the shared gate:
  loads /auth-gate.js, delegates session storage + ?token= exchange +
  401 bouncing to it, keeps SAS-401 red-dot classification local
  because that's EOD-specific.
- index.html, view.html, dump-bin, claims/{,self,investigation,witness},
  shirt-order, suncare/{index,demo-barcodes,endcap-cheat-sheet,
  pallet-cheat-sheet,user-guide}, furniture — all gated by injecting
  <script src="/auth-gate.js"></script> in <head> before any other
  script.
- suncare/sw.js — bump CACHE_NAME to v3 and add skipWaiting +
  clients.claim so installed PWAs pick up the gate-equipped HTML on the
  very next load instead of serving stale cache-first index.html.
- docs/auth.md — how the pieces fit, what's stored where, how to add a
  new gated page, rollback + cutover checklist.

The eod-api backend is unchanged in this commit aside from
FRONTEND_BASE_URL guidance (committed separately in the eod-api repo):
auth-gate.js calls the same /api/{request-link, verify-token,
access-request} endpoints already in place.
